{"id": "DfH6xOcocFu", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why is the KETAKI flower never offered to Shiva? 🌼 Because it once told a LIE, and Shiva himself banned it. (Shiva Purana)\n\nBrahma and Vishnu fought over who was greater. Between them rose a pillar of fire with no end. Vishnu dived for its root, Brahma flew up for its top. Neither found it. On the way, a ketaki fell from Shiva’s head, and Brahma begged it: “Say I saw the top.” The flower lied.\n\nShiva said: “Hereafter I have no desire to include you in my worship.” (Shiva Purana, Vidyeshvara Samhita 8)\n\nThe same Purana bars one more flower: CHAMPA. “Except the Champaka and the Ketaka, there is no flower that does not appeal to Shiva.” (Rudra Samhita 14.36)\n\n🌿 And TULSI? Many say never for Shiva. But the Shiva Purana itself lists tulsi for him: “Worldly pleasures and salvation will be secured by a person who worships with Tulasi.” (Rudra Samhita 14.28). Customs differ, so follow your temple’s priest.\n\n🐘 The god who truly refuses tulsi is GANESHA: Tulsi wished to marry him, he said no, and they cursed each other (Brahma Vaivarta Purana, Ganapati Khanda).\n\n🪷 And the ketaki and champa that Shiva refuses? Vishnu loves them (Narasimha Purana, quoted in the Hari Bhakti Vilasa).\n\n📚 Want your kids to grow up knowing these stories? Our picture books of the gods: Books 1–3, set of 3 for ₹500 at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\n📌 SAVE this before your next puja, SEND it to the person who does puja at home, and COMMENT: did you know tulsi is allowed for Shiva? YES or NO?\n\nNext: what you POUR on Shiva decides what you GET. Follow @therishikatha so you don’t miss it.\n\n#Shiva #Mahadev #ShivaPurana #HarHarMahadev #Ketaki Tulsi Ganesha Vishnu Puja HinduRituals SanatanDharma HinduMythology Shivling Bholenath RishiKatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793374628, "like_count": 6981, "comment_count": 38, "http_headers": {"Referer":